# Grants the active local seat user (systemd-logind ACL, not group/world
# access) read/write on hidraw nodes so VIA/QMK detection and the raw-HID
# VIA protocol can run without root. Same rule VIA and Vial ship themselves
# (see https://www.caniusevia.com/docs/linux) — deliberately broad across
# hidraw rather than scoped to a vendor/usage-page allowlist, since VIA
# detection is itself the thing that tells us whether a given interface is
# safe to talk to; the uaccess tag only ever applies to whoever is logged
# in at the physical seat, not other local users or anything remote.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", TAG+="uaccess"
